[DOCUMENT]
MID: 21f0c18e40ff1a9bcbdebac6ccb9b9f5
TITLE: OCI releases
UID: DOC-VERIFICATION-OCI-RELEASE
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @codexia

[TEXT]
MID: cf22d3272966dfdc73aa874f984184df
STATEMENT: >>>
A repository-local GitHub Actions workflow publishes two independently verified `linux/amd64` images to GHCR when a supported semantic version tag is pushed. Official CLI tags `v0.1.x` are excluded. The image namespace derives from the publishing repository, for example:

- `ghcr.io/<target-owner>/codexia/core:v1.0.0`
- `ghcr.io/<target-owner>/codexia/full:v1.0.0`

The workflow builds each profile from the tagged source, starts the resulting image, checks HTTP/assets/profile, non-root execution, writable data and graceful shutdown, then publishes that same tested image. A failed check prevents that profile from being published. The two profile jobs are independent: a partial release is possible if one fails, and must be treated as incomplete by operators. Do not repoint a published version tag; use a new version for corrections. No `latest` or mutable stable alias is published. Deployment should pin the registry manifest digest resolved from the release tag.

This workflow is intentionally local to Codexia and does not use organization shared release workflows. The GitHub Actions job requires repository Actions permission and GHCR package write access via `GITHUB_TOKEN`. Package visibility is configured separately in GitHub Packages; a public repository does not automatically make new GHCR packages public. Publication requires a release tag to trigger the workflow.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
MID: e11a84037a343f25c0b467a4ee4f50e3
UID: DOC-VERIFICATION-OCI-RELEASE-exact-source-verification-and-immutable-publication
TITLE: Exact-source verification and immutable publication

[TEXT]
MID: a19a0c4a77221dbeae1fe3f646e554c2
STATEMENT: >>>
The shared exact-main verification and release authority is [LINK: DOC-VERIFICATION-CI-CD, CI/CD architecture]. The tag-triggered publisher additionally verifies the tag-to-commit binding immediately before pushing. A tag or PR check alone is insufficient.

[`unpublished-image.mjs`](https://github.com/yohn-jp/codexia/blob/main/scripts/verification/artifacts/unpublished-image.mjs) checks GHCR immediately before each image push. An existing version tag is refused; only a registry 404 with `MANIFEST_UNKNOWN` or `NAME_UNKNOWN` confirms absence. Authorization, service, malformed-response and network failures stop publication. The workflow serializes events for the same Git ref. A partial publication must use a new version; rerunning it must not replace the profile already published.

The tagged OCI publisher uses the repository-local `GITHUB_TOKEN` and rechecks the exact source before publication. Official CLI publication is a distinct workflow and follows [LINK: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-CODEXIACTL-21-cli-自身のリリース更新ライフサイクル正本, the canonical CodexiaCTL release contract], including immutable Releases, artifact attestation and checksum. The CLI release workflow does not require an immutability-read token or a separate publishing App. Neither a tag on a different repository nor its product image is deployment certification evidence for the selected target repository.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
